# [ST09-I S5.7-6 §2 minimal] Cycle-start adjudication, server-authoritative.
# The selector owns the latched /joint_states, the offline FK, the
# scene config, and the latched /vacuum/state; it classifies the
# suction TCP into the container zone taxonomy and reports whether the
# next cycle may start from here. NO route planning rides this service:
# ALREADY_READY means the caller may request GoToRobotPoseV2;
# RECOVERY_REQUIRED is a named stop (the certified exit is the place
# route's own retreat/return legs, or a later recovery route).
# Caller-adopted live identity (RuntimeIdentityV2.scene_revision) —
# the binding check against the selector's own scene.
string scene_revision
---
uint8 ALREADY_READY=1
uint8 RECOVERY_REQUIRED=2
uint8 outcome
string reason_code
# CONTAINER_ZONES classification of the suction TCP (base-link frame;
# "unknown" on identity/FK failure — never a world-frame guess).
string zone
# "carrying" | "unloaded" | "unknown" (latched /vacuum/state.attached;
# an absent feed is unknown, never guessed).
string attachment_state
string detail
